# Store every file exactly as it sits on disk, with no line-ending conversion.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to converting LF to CRLF on checkout and back on
# commit. That is meant to help mixed teams, but on a solo Windows project it
# only creates a class of confusion where a fresh checkout reports every file
# as modified without anybody having touched one. Turning it off means what is
# committed and what is checked out are the same bytes.
#
# If this project ever gains a contributor on macOS or Linux, revisit this -
# that is the situation the default was designed for.
* -text
